(2229008, 304053, 6912, '<td valign="top">thanks everyone, finally even Anastasia has got one ribbon. LOL!<br/> <br/>some people asked me how I did the lighting on that one, it was a very simple trick really, I used pretty long shutterspeed of 1/30 and put my model in front of a huge softbox which made that light, bit overexposed with its purpose as a background. A silver reflector from the left side gave the wings a bit more light to let the structure go thru. And of course I had a wonderful graceful model, who is a professional ball room dancer :-) It helped a lot too...ah...one more thing, we had smth like 4 glasses of wine each before ;-) so it was even more fun.<br/> <br/>here is <br/><a href="//www.pbase.com/anastasija/image/56914286" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">pbase image</a>of the same shop with a bit of spotediting. In the same gallery you can also find the outtakes. And if you like the gallery please vote, I droped from the front page of PBase onto the 2nd one :-)<br/> <br/>your Anastasia the Russki</td>', 'thanks everyone, finally even Anastasia has got one ribbon. LOL! some people asked me how I did the lighting on that one, it was a very simple trick really, I used pretty long shutterspeed of 1/30 and put my model in front of a huge softbox which made that light, bit overexposed with its purpose as a background. A silver reflector from the left side gave the wings a bit more light to let the structure go thru. And of course I had a wonderful graceful model, who is a professional ball room dancer :-) It helped a lot too...ah...one more thing, we had smth like 4 glasses of wine each before ;-) so it was even more fun. here is pbase imageof the same shop with a bit of spotediting. In the same gallery you can also find the outtakes. And if you like the gallery please vote, I droped from the front page of PBase onto the 2nd one :-) your Anastasia the Russki', '2006-03-15 01:32:30.000000', NULL, 0),
